{"id":"mahabharata-3-227","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":227,"title":"सप्तविंशत्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 227 · The pretext of the cattle stations","summary":{"en":"Duryodhana is delighted but knows his father will not allow it. Karna proposes the pretext of inspecting the royal cattle stations near the Dvaita forest, and they all clap hands in agreement.","kn":"ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನು ಹರ್ಷಗೊಂಡರೂ ತಂದೆ ಅನುಮತಿಸನೆಂದು ತಿಳಿದಿದ್ದಾನೆ. ದ್ವೈತವನದ ಬಳಿಯ ರಾಜಗೋಶಾಲೆಗಳ ಪರಿಶೀಲನೆಯ ನೆಪವನ್ನು ಕರ್ಣನು ಸೂಚಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಎಲ್ಲರೂ ಒಪ್ಪಿಗೆಯಿಂದ ಚಪ್ಪಾಳೆ ತಟ್ಟುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"दुर्योधन प्रसन्न होता है पर जानता है कि पिता अनुमति नहीं देंगे। कर्ण द्वैतवन के पास राजकीय गोशालाओं (घोषों) के निरीक्षण का बहाना सुझाता है, और सब सहमति में ताली बजाते हैं।","te":"దుర్యోధనుడు సంతోషించినా తండ్రి అనుమతించడని అతనికి తెలుసు. ద్వైతవనం దగ్గర రాజగోశాలల పరిశీలన అనే నెపాన్ని కర్ణుడు సూచిస్తాడు, అందరూ అంగీకారంతో చప్పట్లు కొడతారు.","ta":"துரியோதனன் மகிழ்ந்தாலும் தந்தை அனுமதிக்க மாட்டார் என்று அறிவான். த்வைத வனத்தருகே உள்ள அரச ஆயர்பாடிகளைப் பார்வையிடுவது என்ற சாக்கைக் கர்ணன் சொல்ல, அனைவரும் ஒப்புதலுடன் கைதட்டுகிறார்கள்.","ml":"ദുര്യോധനൻ സന്തോഷിക്കുന്നുവെങ്കിലും പിതാവ് അനുവദിക്കില്ലെന്ന് അറിയുന്നു. ദ്വൈതവനത്തിനടുത്തുള്ള രാജകീയ കന്നുകാലിത്തൊഴുത്തുകൾ പരിശോധിക്കാനുള്ള ഒരു ഒഴികഴിവ് കർണ്ണൻ നിർദ്ദേശിക്കുന്നു; എല്ലാവരും കയ്യടിച്ച് സമ്മതം അറിയിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.227; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"घोषयात्रापर्व","titleEn":"Ghoshayatra Parva (The cattle expedition)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"कर्णस्य वचनं श्रुत्वा राजा दुर्योधनस्तदा ।\nहृष्टो भूत्वा पुनर्दीन इदं वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Hearing Karna's words, King Duryodhana first rejoiced, then, downcast again, said this.\""}},{"n":2,"text":"ब्रवीषि यदिदं कर्ण सर्वं मे मनसि स्थितम् ।\nन त्वभ्यनुज्ञां लप्स्यामि गमने यत्र पाण्डवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'All that you say, Karna, is in my mind. But I will not get permission to go where the Pandavas are.'\""}},{"n":3,"text":"परिदेवति तान्वीरान्धृतराष्ट्रो महीपतिः ।\nमन्यतेऽभ्यधिकांश्चापि तपोयोगेन पाण्डवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'King Dhritarashtra laments for those heroes and thinks the Pandavas even greater for their austerity.'\""}},{"n":4,"text":"अथ वाप्यनुबुध्येत नृपोऽस्माकं चिकीर्षितम् ।\nएवमप्यायतिं रक्षन्नाभ्यनुज्ञातुमर्हति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Or if the king understood our intention, even guarding the future he would not give us leave.'\""}},{"n":5,"text":"न हि द्वैतवने किंचिद्विद्यतेऽन्यत्प्रयोजनम् ।\nउत्सादनमृते तेषां वनस्थानां मम द्विषाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'For there is no other purpose in Dvaitavana except to ruin those enemies of mine living in the forest.'\""}},{"n":6,"text":"जानासि हि यथा क्षत्ता द्यूतकाल उपस्थिते ।\nअब्रवीद्यच्च मां त्वां च सौबलं च वचस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'You know what Kshatta said to me, to you and to Saubala at the time of the gambling, when it came.'\""}},{"n":7,"text":"तानि पूर्वाणि वाक्यानि यच्चान्यत्परिदेवितम् ।\nविचिन्त्य नाधिगच्छामि गमनायेतराय वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Thinking over those earlier words and the rest of his lament, I cannot decide whether to go or not.'\""}},{"n":8,"text":"ममापि हि महान्हर्षो यदहं भीमफल्गुनौ ।\nक्लिष्टावरण्ये पश्येयं कृष्णया सहिताविति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'I too would have great joy in seeing Bhima and Phalguna in hardship in the forest with Krishna.'\""}},{"n":9,"text":"न तथा प्राप्नुयां प्रीतिमवाप्य वसुधामपि ।\nदृष्ट्वा यथा पाण्डुसुतान्वल्कलाजिनवाससः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'I would not feel such delight even in gaining the earth as in seeing the sons of Pandu dressed in bark and deerskin.'\""}},{"n":10,"text":"किं नु स्यादधिकं तस्माद्यदहं द्रुपदात्मजाम् ।\nद्रौपदीं कर्ण पश्येयं काषायवसनां वने ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'What could be greater than that I should see Drupada's daughter Draupadi, Karna, in the forest dressed in ochre?'\""}},{"n":11,"text":"यदि मां धर्मराजश्च भीमसेनश्च पाण्डवः ।\nयुक्तं परमया लक्ष्म्या पश्येतां जीवितं भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'If Dharmaraja and Bhimasena, the Pandava, should see me joined with supreme glory, my life would be fulfilled.'\""}},{"n":12,"text":"उपायं न तु पश्यामि येन गच्छेम तद्वनम् ।\nयथा चाभ्यनुजानीयाद्गच्छन्तं मां महीपतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'But I see no means by which we might go to that forest, or by which the king would permit me to go.'\""}},{"n":13,"text":"स सौबलेन सहितस्तथा दुःशासनेन च ।\nउपायं पश्य निपुणं येन गच्छेम तद्वनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Together with Saubala and Duhshasana, think out a clever plan by which we may go to that forest.'\""}},{"n":14,"text":"अहमप्यद्य निश्चित्य गमनायेतराय वा ।\nकाल्यमेव गमिष्यामि समीपं पार्थिवस्य ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'I too, having decided today whether to go or not, will go tomorrow morning to the king's presence.'\""}},{"n":15,"text":"मयि तत्रोपविष्टे तु भीष्मे च कुरुसत्तमे ।\nउपायो यो भवेद्दृष्टस्तं ब्रूयाः सहसौबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'When I am seated there with Bhishma, best of the Kurus, tell with Saubala whatever plan you have seen.'\""}},{"n":16,"text":"ततो भीष्मस्य राज्ञश्च निशम्य गमनं प्रति ।\nव्यवसायं करिष्येऽहमनुनीय पितामहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Then, hearing the king and Bhishma about the going, I will settle the matter, having won over my grandfather.'\""}},{"n":17,"text":"तथेत्युक्त्वा तु ते सर्वे जग्मुरावसथान्प्रति ।\nव्युषितायां रजन्यां तु कर्णो राजानमभ्ययात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Saying 'So be it,' they all went to their lodgings. When the night had passed, Karna came to the king.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"ततो दुर्योधनं कर्णः प्रहसन्निदमब्रवीत् ।\nउपायः परिदृष्टोऽयं तं निबोध जनेश्वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then Karna, laughing, said to Duryodhana: 'A plan has been found; hear it, lord of men.'\""}},{"n":19,"text":"घोषा द्वैतवने सर्वे त्वत्प्रतीक्षा नराधिप ।\nघोषयात्रापदेशेन गमिष्यामो न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'The cattle stations are all in Dvaitavana waiting for you, lord of men. Under the pretext of an inspection of the herds, we will certainly go.'\""}},{"n":20,"text":"उचितं हि सदा गन्तुं घोषयात्रां विशां पते ।\nएवं च त्वां पिता राजन्समनुज्ञातुमर्हति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'It is always proper, lord of the people, to go to inspect the herds, and so your father, king, should give you leave.'\""}},{"n":21,"text":"तथा कथयमानौ तौ घोषयात्राविनिश्चयम् ।\nगान्धारराजः शकुनिः प्रत्युवाच हसन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"As they discussed the decision about the inspection, Shakuni, king of Gandhara, answered with a laugh.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"उपायोऽयं मया दृष्टो गमनाय निरामयः ।\nअनुज्ञास्यति नो राजा चोदयिष्यति चाप्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'I have found this safe plan for going. The king will give us leave and even urge us.'\""}},{"n":23,"text":"घोषा द्वैतवने सर्वे त्वत्प्रतीक्षा नराधिप ।\nघोषयात्रापदेशेन गमिष्यामो न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'The cattle stations are all in Dvaitavana waiting for you, lord of men. Under the pretext of an inspection of the herds, we will certainly go.'\""}},{"n":24,"text":"ततः प्रहसिताः सर्वे तेऽन्योन्यस्य तलान्ददुः ।\nतदेव च विनिश्चित्य ददृशुः कुरुसत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then all of them laughed and clapped each other's palms, and having settled on that, they went to see the best of the Kurus.\""}}]}]}